<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17207" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτριβ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not rubbed</i>: hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of places, <i>not
				traversed, pathless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.8
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.257
			</span></i>, al.; of roads, <i>not worn</i> or <i>used,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.2.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Hisp.</u>
				62
			</span></i>: generally, <i>fresh, new,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.3.13
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.7.22
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρ-</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the neck,
				<i>not galled,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Amat.</u>
				134b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ζεύγλης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					37.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not practised in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμικῶν ἀγώνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					3.52
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-βῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					5.145
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
